  "body": "**What happens:** with G54's Z origin placed on the **top** of the part (a common habit, especially on Tormach mills, and what *Set origin* on a top face does), clicking **Milling 2D → 2D Contour** creates nothing. The status line says:\n\n> operation not created: invalid parameters: a 2D Contour operation must cut downward: its top height resolves below its bottom height (check the From references)\n\nThe same applies to every depth kind seeded the same way (pocket, adaptive, offset…).\n\n**Why:** a new operation's heights come from `Carried::of` (`crates/app/src/operation/kinds.rs`). Retyped from the default Face, which has no bottom, the fallback is:\n- `top` = `TopOfModel + 0`\n- `bottom` = `WorkOffset(0) + 0` (the G54 Z0 plane)\n\nWith G54 Z0 at the part top, bottom equals top, so the depth is zero. `CreateOperation` then refuses the operation before the user can open its Heights tab, and the only way through is to move G54 temporarily.\n\n**Expected:** a fresh depth operation is created with a usable default whatever the work-offset convention, and the user then adjusts its heights.\n\n**Proposed fix:** default `bottom` to `BottomOfModel + 0`. It meets the intent of `fresh_depth_operations_default_to_the_part_and_g54` (a fresh operation's numbers show where the material is) without depending on where G54 sits. That test pins the G54 default and would be updated.\n\n**How it was found:** an outside contributor making a Face + 2D Contour job for a Tormach 770MX (#131), with G54 Z on the part top.\n\nSuggested labels (the filer can't set labels): `bug`, `P1`, `area:2d`, `area:ui`, `source:agent`.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n",
